# UI & FRONTEND DEVELOPMENT RULES
- ALWAYS use `css/global.css` for styling. NEVER write inline `<style>` tags or page-specific CSS files unless absolutely necessary for a highly specific widget.
- ALWAYS use the established global design system variables (e.g., `var(--bg-surface)`, `var(--space-md)`, `var(--accent-blue)`).
- ALWAYS use standard layout wrappers: `.enterprise-card`, `.enterprise-layout-2col`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`.
- NEVER remove `id="..."` or `data-*="..."` attributes from HTML elements, as the frontend JavaScript strictly relies on them.
- FORMS: Never let text inputs stretch to 100% width on wide screens; use max-widths.
- SCROLLING: Live video matrixes and map views must never have scrollbars. They must be locked to the viewport height.

# ENTERPRISE FORM & GRID LAYOUT RULES
- STRICT EAST-TO-WEST FORMS: When designing forms with multiple inputs, NEVER stack them in a single massive vertical column on wide screens. ALWAYS use a multi-column CSS Grid: `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(350px, 1fr)); gap: 24px;`.
- NO OVERLAPPING: Form field wrappers must cleanly separate the label and the input. ALWAYS use `display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px;` on the wrapper so the label sits strictly above the input. 
- INPUT WIDTH CAPS: Text inputs, selects, and textareas must NEVER stretch infinitely. ALWAYS apply a max-width (e.g., `max-width: 420px;`).
- LIST ALIGNMENT: Readiness checks and status lists must use `display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;` to keep labels West and statuses East.
- FUNCTIONAL PRESERVATION: Never modify or delete `id`, `data-*`, or `onclick` attributes.

# CREDIT-LEAN-HARD (ME8) — MOB-APPLY CREDIT-LEAN-IN-CURSORRULES-V1
# Disc: docs/MOB-DISC-CREDIT-LEAN-HARD-CODE-20260809.md + docs/MOB-DISC-CREDIT-LEAN-IN-CURSORRULES-20260809.md
