# Violating after CREDIT-LEAN-HARD = failure.

# UI COPY PROFESSIONAL (ME8) — always — WHOLE SOFTWARE
# Disc: docs/MOB-DISC-UI-COPY-TEACH-STRIP-JUDGMENT-CONCEPT-20260810.md
#        docs/MOB-DISC-UI-COPY-INDUSTRY-NO-PERMANENT-TEACH-STRIP-20260810.md
# Rule: .cursor/rules/me8-ui-copy-professional.mdc
#
# Concept (agent owns judgment — operator does NOT memorize key lists):
#   A) Working page + clear title → REMOVE permanent teach strip (no “what this is / don’t open…”).
#   B) Rare / high-risk / IT misconfig risk → KEEP one short industry one-liner beside the control.
#   C) Empty / error / confirm / modal gate / once-wizard → KEEP short factual.
# Manuals = full teach. Not “hide all help” and not “essay on every page”.
# Copy = words/visibility only. Before whole-UI Grep: ASK permission.
# APPLY judgment pass: MOB-APPLY UI-COPY-PANEL-INTRO-JUDGMENT-V1

# NEVER send absolute backend paths to the client (ME8)
# Disc: path disclosure (folderHint / ftpRoot / STORAGE_DIR / open-folder)

FORBIDDEN in res.json, res.send, HTML/EJS, i18n strings filled from the server, and operator toasts:
- __dirname, process.cwd(), BASE_DIR, STORAGE_DIR, FTP_ROOT, FR_STORAGE_ROOT
- path.resolve / path.normalize / path.join results that are absolute
- folderHint, serverPath, absolutePath, storagePath, ftpRoot, liveCaptureRoot,
  mountFull, configuredRoot, activeRoot, fleetLog, backups.dir, browse entry.path
  when those values are OS absolute (C:\…, /var/, /opt/, /usr/, /home/, UNC)

ALLOWED to the client:
- install-relative labels only, via a helper that never returns an absolute path
  (e.g. storage/ftp-uploads, storage/fr-kept). If the folder is outside the
  install tree, send a role label ("Network archive" / "Custom folder") — never
  the raw mount.
- Super-admin path *input* fields the operator typed themselves (save what they
  entered; do not echo resolved fs.realpath).
- Super-admin browse-paths stays behind requireSuperAdmin; do not reuse that
  payload on operator pages.

Errors: always opErr() / operatorErrorVoice.jsonErr. NEVER err.message, err.stack,
or String(err) in a client body.

Logs may keep full paths server-side only.

